# PowerEngine dashboard: managed by the PowerEngine app.
# This file is rewritten whenever PowerEngine is updated; local edits will be lost.
# Needs: Power Flow Card Plus and ApexCharts Card (HACS). See docs/INSTALL.md, Step 5.
title: Power Engine
views:
  - title: Monitoring
    path: monitoring
    icon: mdi:lightning-bolt
    type: sections
    max_columns: 3
    sections:
      - type: grid
        column_span: 3
        cards:
          - type: markdown
            grid_options: {columns: full}
            content: |-
              {% set t = state_attr('sensor.pe_state_summary', 'text') or states('sensor.pe_state_summary') %}
              {% set parts = t.split('. ', 1) %}
              **{{ parts[0] }}**{% if parts | count > 1 %} {{ parts[1] }}{% endif %}
          - type: tile
            entity: sensor.pe_state_operation_mode
            name: Mode
            grid_options: {columns: 4}
          - type: tile
            entity: sensor.pe_state_decision
            name: Decision
            grid_options: {columns: 4}
          - type: tile
            entity: sensor.pe_state_battery_soc
            name: Battery
            grid_options: {columns: 4}
            features:
              - type: bar-gauge
      - type: grid
        column_span: 2
        cards:
          - type: heading
            heading: Energy flow
          - type: custom:power-flow-card-plus
            grid_options: {columns: full}
            watt_threshold: 1000
            kw_decimals: 1
            min_flow_rate: 1
            max_flow_rate: 6
            clickable_entities: true
            display_zero_lines:
              mode: transparency
              transparency: 70
            entities:
              battery:
                entity: sensor.pe_state_battery_power
                state_of_charge: sensor.pe_state_battery_soc
              grid:
                entity: sensor.pe_state_grid_power
              solar:
                entity: sensor.pe_state_solar_power
                display_zero_state: true
              home:
                entity: sensor.pe_state_house_power
                override_state: true
              individual:
                - entity: sensor.pe_state_ev_power
                  name: Car
                  icon: mdi:car-electric
                  display_zero: true
                  display_zero_tolerance: 50
      - type: grid
        cards:
          - type: heading
            heading: Now
          - type: markdown
            content: |-
              {% set imp = state_attr('sensor.pe_state_import_rate', 'pence') %}
              {% set until = state_attr('sensor.pe_state_import_rate', 'until') %}
              {% set nxt = state_attr('sensor.pe_state_import_rate', 'next_rate_pence') %}
              {% set exp = state_attr('sensor.pe_state_export_rate', 'pence') %}
              **Import** {{ imp if imp is not none else '–' }}p
              {%- if state_attr('sensor.pe_state_import_rate', 'in_smart_slot') %} (smart slot){% endif %}
              {%- if until and nxt is not none %}, then {{ nxt }}p from {{ until }}{% endif %}

              **Export** {{ exp if exp is not none else '–' }}p
          - type: tile
            entity: sensor.pe_state_ev
            name: Car
          - type: tile
            entity: sensor.pe_state_smart_charge
            name: EDF smart charge
          - type: tile
            entity: sensor.pe_state_axle
            name: Axle
          - type: tile
            entity: sensor.pe_state_free_power
            name: Free power
          - type: markdown
            content: |-
              {% set t = state_attr('sensor.pe_state_solar_power', 'forecast_today_kwh') %}
              {% set m = state_attr('sensor.pe_state_solar_power', 'forecast_tomorrow_kwh') %}
              **Solar forecast** today {{ t if t is not none else '–' }} kWh · tomorrow {{ m if m is not none else '–' }} kWh
      - type: grid
        column_span: 3
        cards:
          - type: heading
            heading: Activity
          - type: markdown
            grid_options: {columns: full}
            content: |-
              {% set entries = state_attr('sensor.pe_state_activity', 'entries') or [] %}
              {%- if entries | count == 0 %}No decisions yet.{% endif %}
              {%- for e in entries[:8] %}
              - **{{ e.hhmm }}** {{ e.text }}
              {%- endfor %}
      - type: grid
        column_span: 3
        cards:
          - type: heading
            heading: Last 24 hours
          - type: history-graph
            grid_options: {columns: full}
            hours_to_show: 24
            entities:
              - entity: sensor.pe_state_solar_power
                name: Solar
              - entity: sensor.pe_state_house_power
                name: House
              - entity: sensor.pe_state_battery_power
                name: Battery (+ discharging)
              - entity: sensor.pe_state_grid_power
                name: Grid (+ importing)
              - entity: sensor.pe_state_ev_power
                name: Car
          - type: history-graph
            grid_options: {columns: full}
            hours_to_show: 24
            entities:
              - entity: sensor.pe_state_battery_soc
                name: Battery % (real)
              - entity: sensor.pe_state_sim_soc
                name: Battery % (PowerEngine simulated)
      - type: grid
        column_span: 3
        cards:
          - type: heading
            heading: PowerEngine health
            heading_style: subtitle
          - type: tile
            entity: sensor.pe_diag_heartbeat
            name: Heartbeat
            grid_options: {columns: 4}
          - type: tile
            entity: binary_sensor.pe_diag_config_ok
            name: Config OK
            grid_options: {columns: 4}
          - type: tile
            entity: sensor.pe_diag_version
            name: Version
            grid_options: {columns: 4}
  - title: Plan
    path: plan
    icon: mdi:calendar-clock
    type: sections
    max_columns: 3
    sections:
      - type: grid
        column_span: 3
        cards:
          - type: markdown
            grid_options: {columns: full}
            content: |-
              {% set made = states('sensor.pe_plan') -%}
              **{{ state_attr('sensor.pe_plan_headline', 'text') or 'No plan yet.' }}**

              Plan made {{ as_timestamp(made) | timestamp_custom('%H:%M') if made not in ['unknown', 'unavailable', ''] else '–' }}
              · re-plans every 5 minutes and when prices, slots or events change
              · house load learned from {{ state_attr('sensor.pe_plan', 'load_profile_days') or 0 }} days of history
              {%- if (state_attr('sensor.pe_plan', 'load_profile_days') or 0) < 2 %}
              · **the load forecast is still learning**, so treat this plan as rough for the first day or two{% endif %}
              {%- macro money(v) -%}{% set v = v | float(0) %}{{ ('earns £%.2f' | format(-v)) if v < -0.005 else ('costs £%.2f' | format(v)) }}{%- endmacro %}
              · this plan {{ money(state_attr('sensor.pe_plan', 'cost')) }} over the period; plain self-use {{ money(state_attr('sensor.pe_plan', 'baseline_cost')) }}
              {%- set extra = state_attr('sensor.pe_plan', 'extra_kwh') | float(0) %}{% if extra | abs >= 0.5 %}
              · the plan ends with {{ '%.1f' | format(extra | abs) }} kWh {{ 'more' if extra > 0 else 'less' }} in the battery than plain self-use (worth £{{ '%.2f' | format(state_attr('sensor.pe_plan', 'extra_value') | float(0) | abs) }} at the cheapest price), counted in the saving{% endif %}
              {%- if state_attr('sensor.pe_plan', 'estimated_prices_from') %}
              · prices after {{ as_timestamp(state_attr('sensor.pe_plan', 'estimated_prices_from')) | timestamp_custom('%a %H:%M') }} are estimated (not yet published){% endif %}
          - type: custom:apexcharts-card
            grid_options: {columns: full, rows: auto}
            graph_span: 36h
            span:
              start: minute
            now:
              show: true
              label: Now
            header:
              show: true
              title: Next 36 hours
              show_states: false
            apex_config:
              chart: {height: 380}
              legend: {show: true}
              tooltip: {shared: true}
            yaxis:
              # each axis is drawn in the colour of what it measures
              - id: soc
                min: 0
                max: 100
                decimals: 0
                apex_config:
                  title: {text: "Battery %", style: {color: "#43a047"}}
                  labels: {style: {colors: "#43a047"}}
                  axisBorder: {show: true, color: "#43a047", width: 3}
              - id: price
                opposite: true
                min: 0
                decimals: 0
                apex_config:
                  title: {text: "Import price p/kWh", style: {color: "#fb8c00"}}
                  labels: {style: {colors: "#fb8c00"}}
                  axisBorder: {show: true, color: "#fb8c00", width: 3}
              - id: kwh
                opposite: true
                min: 0
                decimals: 1
                apex_config:
                  title: {text: "kWh per half-hour (solar, load, charge)", style: {color: "#1e88e5"}}
                  labels: {style: {colors: "#1e88e5"}}
                  axisBorder: {show: true, color: "#1e88e5", width: 3}
            series:
              - entity: sensor.pe_plan
                name: Battery (planned)
                yaxis_id: soc
                type: line
                color: "#43a047"
                stroke_width: 3
                extend_to: false
                data_generator: |
                  const s = entity.attributes.series || {t: []};
                  return s.t.map((t, i) => [new Date(t).getTime() + 1800000, s.soc[i]]);
              - entity: sensor.pe_plan
                name: Import price
                yaxis_id: price
                type: line
                curve: stepline
                color: "#fb8c00"
                stroke_width: 2
                extend_to: false
                data_generator: |
                  const s = entity.attributes.series || {t: []};
                  return s.t.map((t, i) => [new Date(t).getTime(), s.price_p[i]]);
              - entity: sensor.pe_plan
                name: Solar forecast (kWh)
                yaxis_id: kwh
                type: area
                color: "#fdd835"
                opacity: 0.3
                extend_to: false
                data_generator: |
                  const s = entity.attributes.series || {t: []};
                  return s.t.map((t, i) => [new Date(t).getTime(), s.solar_kwh[i]]);
              - entity: sensor.pe_plan
                name: House load forecast (kWh)
                yaxis_id: kwh
                type: line
                color: "#9e9e9e"
                stroke_width: 1
                extend_to: false
                data_generator: |
                  const s = entity.attributes.series || {t: []};
                  return s.t.map((t, i) => [new Date(t).getTime(), s.load_kwh[i]]);
              - entity: sensor.pe_plan
                name: Grid charge (kWh)
                yaxis_id: kwh
                type: area
                curve: stepline
                opacity: 0.6
                stroke_width: 1
                color: "#1e88e5"
                extend_to: false
                # a block spanning each half-hour (not a thin bar at its start)
                data_generator: |
                  const s = entity.attributes.series || {t: []};
                  const pts = s.t.map((t, i) => [new Date(t).getTime(), s.charge_kwh[i]]);
                  if (pts.length) pts.push([pts[pts.length - 1][0] + 1800000, 0]);
                  return pts;
              - entity: sensor.pe_plan
                name: Axle export (kWh)
                yaxis_id: kwh
                type: area
                curve: stepline
                opacity: 0.6
                stroke_width: 1
                color: "#e53935"
                extend_to: false
                # a block spanning each half-hour (not a thin bar at its start)
                data_generator: |
                  const s = entity.attributes.series || {t: []};
                  const pts = s.t.map((t, i) => [new Date(t).getTime(), s.discharge_kwh[i]]);
                  if (pts.length) pts.push([pts[pts.length - 1][0] + 1800000, 0]);
                  return pts;
      - type: grid
        column_span: 3
        cards:
          - type: heading
            heading: Actions
          - type: markdown
            grid_options: {columns: full}
            content: |-
              | Time | Action | Target | Price | Battery | Why |
              |---|---|---|---|---|---|
              {%- for w in state_attr('sensor.pe_plan', 'windows') or [] %}
              | {{ (w.day ~ ' ') if w.day }}{{ w.from }}–{{ w.to }} | **{{ w.action | replace('_', '-') }}** | {{ (w.target_soc | int | string ~ '%') if w.target_soc else '–' }} | {{ w.price }}{{ ' (est.)' if w.estimated else '' }} | {{ w.soc_start }}% → {{ w.soc_end }}% | {{ w.reason }} |
              {%- endfor %}
  - title: Costs
    path: costs
    icon: mdi:cash-multiple
    type: sections
    max_columns: 3
    sections:
      - type: grid
        column_span: 3
        cards:
          # title on the left, a small alignment switch on the right (from the PowerEngine card bundle)
          - type: custom:powerengine-toggle-card
            title: Costs
            entity: switch.pe_ui_right_align
            name: Alignment
            grid_options: {columns: full, rows: 1}
          - type: markdown
            grid_options: {columns: full}
            content: |-
              {%- macro gbp(v) -%}{% set v = v | float(0) %}{{ ('−£%.2f' | format(-v)) if v < -0.005 else ('£%.2f' | format(v | abs if v | abs < 0.005 else v)) }}{%- endmacro %}
              {%- set days = state_attr('sensor.pe_cost_days', 'days') or [] %}
              {%- set done = days | selectattr('complete') | list %}
              {%- if done %}{% set y = done | last %}
              **{{ as_timestamp(y.date) | timestamp_custom('%a %d %b') }}: {{ gbp(y.actual) }} actual vs {{ gbp(y.s0) }} with no solar or battery.** Solar saved {{ gbp(y.solar) }}, smart charge {{ gbp(y.smart) }}, battery {{ gbp(y.s3a) }} (default) + {{ gbp(y.s3b) }} (control), arbitrage {{ gbp(y.arbitrage) }}.
              {%- else %}
              **No complete days yet.** PowerEngine counts forward from when 0.4 was installed; the first full day appears after midnight.
              {%- endif %}
              {%- set t = states.sensor.pe_cost_today %}
              {%- if t and t.attributes.actual is defined %}

              Today so far: {{ gbp(t.attributes.actual) }} actual vs {{ gbp(t.attributes.s0) }} with no solar or battery ({{ t.attributes.half_hours }} half-hour{{ '' if t.attributes.half_hours == 1 else 's' }} recorded).
              {%- endif %}
              {%- if done and (done | last).coverage < 0.95 %}

              PowerEngine was recording for {{ ((done | last).coverage * 100) | round(0) | int }}% of that day (restarts or gaps), so the day's figures are partial.
              {%- endif %}
          - type: custom:apexcharts-card
            grid_options: {columns: full, rows: auto}
            graph_span: 8d
            span:
              end: day
              offset: "-12h"
            header:
              show: true
              title: Daily cost, step by step
              show_states: false
            apex_config:
              chart: {height: 380}
              legend: {show: true}
              tooltip: {shared: true}
              xaxis: {labels: {format: "ddd dd"}}
            yaxis:
              - decimals: 2
                apex_config: {title: {text: "£ per day"}}
            series:
              - entity: sensor.pe_cost_days
                show: {legend_value: false}
                name: "S0: no solar or battery"
                type: column
                color: "#8d6e63"
                extend_to: false
                data_generator: |
                  const from = Date.now() - 8 * 86400000;
                  return (entity.attributes.days || []).map(d => [new Date(d.date + "T00:00:00").getTime(), d.steps[0][1]]).filter(p => p[0] >= from);
              - entity: sensor.pe_cost_days
                show: {legend_value: false}
                name: "S1: + solar"
                type: column
                color: "#fdd835"
                extend_to: false
                data_generator: |
                  const from = Date.now() - 8 * 86400000;
                  return (entity.attributes.days || []).map(d => [new Date(d.date + "T00:00:00").getTime(), d.steps[1][1]]).filter(p => p[0] >= from);
              - entity: sensor.pe_cost_days
                show: {legend_value: false}
                name: "S2: + smart charge"
                type: column
                color: "#26a69a"
                extend_to: false
                data_generator: |
                  const from = Date.now() - 8 * 86400000;
                  return (entity.attributes.days || []).map(d => [new Date(d.date + "T00:00:00").getTime(), d.steps[2][1]]).filter(p => p[0] >= from);
              - entity: sensor.pe_cost_days
                show: {legend_value: false}
                name: "S3a: + battery (default)"
                type: column
                color: "#42a5f5"
                extend_to: false
                data_generator: |
                  const from = Date.now() - 8 * 86400000;
                  return (entity.attributes.days || []).map(d => [new Date(d.date + "T00:00:00").getTime(), d.steps[3][1]]).filter(p => p[0] >= from);
              - entity: sensor.pe_cost_days
                show: {legend_value: false}
                name: "S3b: + battery control"
                type: column
                color: "#1e88e5"
                extend_to: false
                data_generator: |
                  const from = Date.now() - 8 * 86400000;
                  return (entity.attributes.days || []).map(d => [new Date(d.date + "T00:00:00").getTime(), d.steps[4][1]]).filter(p => p[0] >= from);
              - entity: sensor.pe_cost_days
                show: {legend_value: false}
                name: "S4: + battery export (arbitrage)"
                type: column
                color: "#ab47bc"
                extend_to: false
                data_generator: |
                  const from = Date.now() - 8 * 86400000;
                  return (entity.attributes.days || []).map(d => [new Date(d.date + "T00:00:00").getTime(), d.steps[5][1]]).filter(p => p[0] >= from);
              - entity: sensor.pe_cost_days
                show: {legend_value: false}
                name: "Actual"
                type: column
                color: "#424242"
                extend_to: false
                data_generator: |
                  const from = Date.now() - 8 * 86400000;
                  return (entity.attributes.days || []).map(d => [new Date(d.date + "T00:00:00").getTime(), d.steps[7][1]]).filter(p => p[0] >= from);
      - type: grid
        column_span: 3
        cards:
          - type: heading
            heading: By day
          - type: markdown
            grid_options: {columns: full}
            content: |-
              {%- macro gbp(v) -%}{% set v = v | float(0) %}{{ ('−£%.2f' | format(-v)) if v < -0.005 else ('£%.2f' | format(v | abs if v | abs < 0.005 else v)) }}{%- endmacro %}
              {%- set a = '---' if is_state('switch.pe_ui_right_align', 'off') else '---:' %}
              | Day | No solar/battery | Solar | Smart | Battery (default) | Battery control | Arbitrage | Carried in battery | Actual | Unexplained |
              |---|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|
              {%- for d in (state_attr('sensor.pe_cost_days', 'days') or []) | reverse %}
              | {{ as_timestamp(d.date) | timestamp_custom('%a %d %b') }}{{ ' (so far)' if not d.complete else '' }} | {{ gbp(d.s0) }} | {{ gbp(d.solar) }} | {{ gbp(d.smart) }} | {{ gbp(d.s3a) }} | {{ gbp(d.s3b) }} | {{ gbp(d.arbitrage) }} | {{ gbp(d.stored) }} | **{{ gbp(d.actual) }}** | {{ gbp(d.unexplained) }} |
              {%- endfor %}

              Savings columns reduce the cost; "Carried in battery" is energy bought or stored for later use (it adds to today's cost and is credited when used). {% if states('sensor.pe_state_operation_mode') != 'active' %}PowerEngine is in Passive mode, so "Battery control" and "Arbitrage" show what your current setup (for example Predbat or your automations) actually did, not PowerEngine.{% endif %}
          - type: heading
            heading: Energy by day
          - type: markdown
            grid_options: {columns: full}
            content: |-
              {%- macro k(v) -%}{{ '%.1f' | format(v | float(0)) }}{%- endmacro %}
              {%- set a = '---' if is_state('switch.pe_ui_right_align', 'off') else '---:' %}
              | Day | Import | Export | Solar | House | Car | Battery in | Battery out | Battery → export | Unaccounted | Ledger correction |
              |---|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|
              {%- for d in (state_attr('sensor.pe_cost_days', 'days') or []) | reverse %}{% set e = d.energy or {} %}
              | {{ as_timestamp(d.date) | timestamp_custom('%a %d %b') }} | {{ k(e.grid_import) }} | {{ k(e.grid_export) }} | {{ k(e.solar) }} | {{ k(e.house) }} | {{ k(e.car) }} | {{ k(e.battery_in) }} | {{ k(e.battery_out) }} | {{ k(e.b_e) }} | {{ k(e.unallocated_src) }} | {{ k(e.correction_kwh) }} |
              {%- endfor %}

              kWh, integrated from the 30-second readings. Compare with the inverter's daily counters to check the sensors. *Unaccounted* is energy supplied (solar, grid, battery) that didn't reach a measured destination: inverter losses, standby and sensor mismatch. It is the main source of *Unexplained* cost. *Ledger correction* is how far the battery's real state of charge differed from what the flows predicted.
          - type: heading
            heading: Special events
          - type: markdown
            grid_options: {columns: full}
            content: |-
              {%- macro gbp(v) -%}{% set v = v | float(0) %}{{ ('−£%.2f' | format(-v)) if v < -0.005 else ('£%.2f' | format(v | abs if v | abs < 0.005 else v)) }}{%- endmacro %}
              {%- set a = '---' if is_state('switch.pe_ui_right_align', 'off') else '---:' %}
              {%- set e = states.sensor.pe_event_last %}
              {%- if e and e.attributes.type is defined %}
              **Last event:** {{ 'Axle export' if e.attributes.type == 'axle' else 'Free power' }} on {{ as_timestamp(e.attributes.date) | timestamp_custom('%a %d %b') }} from {{ e.attributes.time }}: {{ e.attributes.kwh }} kWh, worth {{ gbp(e.attributes.gross) }} ({{ gbp(e.attributes.net) }} net).
              {%- else %}
              No Axle or free-power events recorded yet.
              {%- endif %}

              | Month | Axle (net) | Free power (net) | Everyday actual |
              |---|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|{{ a }}|
              {%- for m in (state_attr('sensor.pe_event_months', 'months') or []) | reverse %}
              | {{ as_timestamp(m.month ~ '-01') | timestamp_custom('%b %Y') }} | {{ gbp(m.axle_net) }} | {{ gbp(m.free_power_net) }} | {{ gbp(m.actual) }} |
              {%- endfor %}

              Axle and free-power half-hours are kept out of the daily layers above so rare, large events don't distort them. Net value is what the event added: Axle kWh × £1, less what that energy was worth (its cost in the battery, or the export rate); free power is the kWh used × the rate that would otherwise have applied.
      - type: grid
        column_span: 3
        cards:
          - type: heading
            heading: How these numbers are calculated
          - type: markdown
            grid_options: {columns: full}
            content: |-
              Each half-hour, PowerEngine splits the energy into flows: solar, battery and grid supplying the house, the car, the battery and export (solar first, then battery, then grid). Each flow is valued at that half-hour's rates.

              - **No solar or battery (S0):** house kWh × standard rate + car kWh × overnight rate + standing charge. Assumes the car would otherwise have charged overnight.
              - **Solar:** solar used by the house × standard rate, plus solar exported or stored × export rate.
              - **Smart charge:** every kWh bought in an EDF smart slot × (standard rate − slot rate), split between house, car (against the overnight rate) and battery by where it went. The standard rate in a slot is the day's peak rate.
              - **Battery (default):** a half-hour simulation of the inverter's plain self-use with the same battery: charges only from surplus solar, covers the house.
              - **Battery control:** the battery's real value minus the default: what the charge/discharge timing added. Energy delivered is valued at the rate it avoided; energy used is costed from a first-in-first-out ledger (solar at the export rate, grid at the standard rate when bought), losses included. Can be negative. In Passive mode this is whatever is controlling the battery today.
              - **Arbitrage:** grid-bought energy later exported: export revenue − its cost.
              - **Carried in battery:** the change in the ledger's value: energy bought or stored today for later. The ledger is matched to the battery's real state of charge every half-hour; any correction shows in Unexplained.
              - **Actual:** metered import × rate − metered export × export rate + standing charge.
              - **Unexplained:** Actual minus the layers. Inverter losses, standby use and meter mismatch land here; if it grows, the model needs fixing.

              Caveats: half-hour resolution from HA's sensors, which may differ slightly from EDF's bill; rates are the ones seen at the time; first-in-first-out is a convention, not physics; battery round-trip efficiency is {{ states('sensor.pe_diag_battery_efficiency') }}% ({{ 'measured over the last 30 days' if state_attr('sensor.pe_diag_battery_efficiency', 'measured') else 'the configured figure until 14 full days are recorded' }}). Method version {{ state_attr('sensor.pe_cost_days', 'method') or 1 }}.
  - title: Config
    path: config
    icon: mdi:cog
    panel: true
    cards:
      - type: custom:powerengine-config-card
